      "statusChangeID": "5eea9f2a4e7a29475dd65c66",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Unfortunately, this is not a bug.\nTransparency is not permitted on avatars on Oculus Quest, as it is highly imperformant on the platform. This new behavior (transparency not working) is actually the correct behavior. \nIn 2020.2.2, we fixed a bug where material validation was not properly inspecting particle materials. This means that transparency will no longer work on particles on Oculus Quest.\nThere is potential for us to explicitly allow alpha transparency on avatar particles in the future, but we must consider performance impact first.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
